IMU daemon — attitude, heading, and heave for boats ("gpsd for IMUs")
 imud reads an I2C IMU and magnetometer, fuses them with a quaternion
 Multiplicative EKF, and serves attitude, heading (magnetic and WMM true),
 rate of turn, heave, and sea-state statistics to the network: NMEA 0183
 over UDP, a high-rate binary UDP stream, and a local AF_UNIX subscription
 socket. A built-in black box can record every raw sensor sample to .imucap
 capture files, and the sim driver replays them (or a synthetic scenario)
 through the full pipeline.
 .
 Includes calibration and self-characterization (imud-cal), a status tool
 (imud-status), the Python client, and a hardened systemd service. The
 network monitor ships as imud-utils; protocol bridges are packaged
 separately: imud-signalk, imud-mqtt, imud-influxdb, imud-mavlink,
 imud-prometheus.
